# Unreal Engine — standard ignores.
# Generated/derived directories: never commit these.
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Build/
Platforms/*/Binaries/
Platforms/*/Intermediate/

# IDE / project files (regenerated by GenerateProjectFiles)
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
*.sln
*.suo
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?

# Crash/automation artifacts
Saved/Crashes/
Saved/Logs/

# Cooked/packaged output
Packaged/
Dist/

# ===========================================================================
# THIRD-PARTY PAID / LICENSED ASSETS — NEVER COMMIT TO PUBLIC HISTORY.
# Per sibelius-game-asset-license-policy.md (walt-cowork-memory).
# The compiled Steam build is the licensed distribution channel; the public
# repo is source + open content only. Each developer must install these
# locally from Fab after their own purchase.
#
# These rules MUST exist BEFORE any paid asset enters the working tree —
# git history cannot be cleanly scrubbed after a push (see policy doc).
# Over-inclusive on purpose: an extra entry is harmless, a missing entry
# is a license leak. The post-install `git status` check is the safety net.
# ===========================================================================

# --- QuadArt packs: House Furniture + Modular House ---
#     Standard tier, purchased 2026-05-27. Written AI-use permission on file
#     (quadarthelp@gmail.com, 2026-05-26). Chapter 1 environment ONLY.
# EasyBiomes poplar kit — PAID, parked, do not delete, do not use in the game.
# See docs/FORESTS_DO_NOT_USE.md (Walt 2026-08-19).
Content/EasyBiomes/
Content/QuadArt/
Content/QuadArt_*/
Content/*QuadArt*/
Content/HouseFurniture/
Content/House_Furniture/
Content/HouseFurniturePack/
Content/ModularHouse/
Content/Modular_House/
Content/ModularHouses/
Content/ModularHousePack/

# --- Crebotoly modular sci-fi kits (SIB-47 Sauce Door "Server Cathedral") ---
#     Four kits, purchased from Fab. Referenced by asset path only; bytes stay
#     local (install via Fab -> Add to Project). The DataTable/CSV that point at
#     them ARE committed (they're our content, not the kit).
Content/ModularSciFiEnv_*/
Content/Crebotoly*/

# --- SciFi prop kits (SIB-47 scatter): boxes / crates / containers / barrels ---
#     "SciFi Boxes A" and "SciFi Boxes B" packs, purchased from Fab. Same policy as
#     the Crebotoly kits: referenced by /Game/... path only, bytes stay local (Fab
#     install). Note the two different on-disk folder names the packs ship with.
Content/SciFiBoxes_A/
Content/SciFiBoxes_B/
Content/SciFi_Box_A/
Content/SciFi_Box_B/
Content/SciFiBox_*/
Content/SciFi_Boxes_*/

# --- PN (Project Nature) foliage packs (SIB Forest Elsewhere) ---
#     Spruce forest, grass, open-world foliage, foliage collection — purchased from Fab,
#     ~4.2 GB. Same policy as the Crebotoly/SciFi kits: referenced by /Game/... path only
#     (the PCG forest graph + grass material point at them); bytes stay local (Fab install).
Content/PN_interactiveSpruceForest/
Content/PN_GrassLibrary/
Content/PN_OpenWorldFoliage/
Content/PN_FoliageCollection/
Content/PN_*/

# Downtown West Modular Pack (PurePolygons, free from Epic) - VENDOR, 12 GB on disk.
# L_City is duplicated OUT of its demo map into Content/Maps and IS committed; the pack
# itself stays out of the repo like every other vendor pack here. It reaches the player
# through the cook, which follows references from L_City - 12 GB of source becomes about
# 1 GB of pak. Re-install from Fab if a fresh clone needs it.
Content/Downtown_West/

# Phantom All In One (Pautinka, PAID) - the ghost/energy material pack the AI ghosts
# in L_City are made of. Vendor, licensed to the buying Epic account, and this repo is
# public - so the pack stays out of it.
#
# Content/Phantom/ is NOT ignored: that folder holds Manny_Glow, Walt's own tuned
# Material Instance, and it is the only part of the look that is his. Its PARENT
# material lives in the pack, so a fresh clone gets a broken reference until the pack is
# re-downloaded - the same deal as every other entry in docs/VENDOR_PACKS.md.
Content/Phantom_All_In_One/

# Coffee Shop / RestaurantScene (Leartes Studios) - the cafe interior behind the deli
# door in the city. FREE to download from Fab, which is not the same as free to
# REDISTRIBUTE: the Standard License grants use, not publication, and this repo is
# public. Out it goes, like every other pack.
Content/RestaurantScene/

# Rocket Launch Pad & Interior (PackDev) - the spaceport Generate builds on the lawn,
# and the rocket Phase C will launch. Bought for $39.99, which buys USE and not
# REDISTRIBUTION: this repo is public, so committing 23 meshes and their 4K textures
# would be publishing a paid pack. Same rule as every other entry above.
#
# It reaches the shipped pak through DirectoriesToAlwaysCook in DefaultGame.ini, exactly
# like the sci-fi packs - Spaceport.cpp names its meshes by soft path, and a soft path in
# C++ is not a package reference the cooker will follow.
Content/Rocket_Launch_Pad/

# ...and the same pack SPILLS its showcase cinematic outside its own folder, into the
# project's shared Cinematics directory next to the Kaia intro. Only the Sequences
# subfolder is vendor; Content/Cinematics itself holds L_Cine_KaiaIntro, L_Meadow and
# LS_Kaia_Intro and must stay tracked.
Content/Cinematics/Sequences/
Content/__ExternalActors__/RestaurantScene/
Content/__ExternalObjects__/RestaurantScene/
Content/__ExternalActors__/Phantom_All_In_One/
Content/__ExternalObjects__/Phantom_All_In_One/

# Build logs from Build.bat runs (pkg-v*.log is already covered above).
build-*.log

# --- Marketplace character / creature packs (Epic + Fab, re-downloadable from the
#     account library). These predate the ignore policy and were tracked by accident:
#     ~5.1 GB of LFS, the largest single block in the repo. Verified pristine — each
#     arrived in exactly one import commit and was never edited, so nothing here is
#     ours to lose. Same policy as the Crebotoly/SciFi/PN kits: referenced by
#     /Game/... path only, bytes stay local. Untracking stops further LFS growth;
#     the copies already pushed remain in history until a deliberate rewrite.
Content/ParagonGreystone/
Content/EchoContent/
Content/AfricanAnimalsPack/
Content/AnimalVarietyPack/
Content/FarmKeepers/

# --- Mocap / animation packs (Fab, re-downloadable from the account library) ---
#     Track the MACHINE, not the MATERIAL. The IK Rig and the IK Retargeter under
#     Content/Characters/Retargeting/ are configuration WE authored against our own
#     SKM_Manny_Simple — no vendor data in them — so they stay tracked and the
#     pipeline survives a fresh clone. The retargeted OUTPUT does not: resampling
#     mocap onto another skeleton does not make it ours, and this repo is public.
#     Never build a tracked asset that references a path in here.
Content/MorroMotion/
Content/XenoMocap/
# Retargeted output — vendor motion on our skeleton. Local only; re-export from
# RTG_Mannequin_to_MetaHuman after re-downloading the source pack.
Content/Characters/Retargeting/Anims/
Content/Characters/Retargeting/*_MH.uasset
# The Morro Motion installer also drops raw FBX at the PROJECT ROOT, outside
# Content/ entirely — 50 MB that no ignore rule was covering. Same vendor bytes.
Anim_Source/

# --- Generic paid-asset zones (policy's predefined partition) ---
Content/Paid/
Content/Fab/
Content/Megascans/
Content/Environment/Megascans/
Content/Environment/Cathedral/
Content/Environment/Office/Paid/
Content/Props/Paid/

# --- MetaHuman source (Epic discourages public-source redistribution) ---
Content/Characters/Leonard/
# Ignore the MetaHuman *source* assets but keep the reconstruction note tracked.
# (Must ignore contents with /*, not the dir itself, so the README can be re-included.)
Content/MetaHumans/*
!Content/MetaHumans/README.md

# --- AI-generated audio/video (vendor licenses don't authorize public source) ---
Content/Audio/Generated/
Content/Music/Generated/
Content/Cinematics/Generated/
# Mrs. Hall refusal voice clips (SIB-30 P2.5) — AI-generated (ElevenLabs etc.); local-only,
# back up manually. Regenerable from the Line->AudioKey manifest. Clear the synthetic-voice
# commercial license before any shipped build.
Content/Audio/MrsHall/
# Dancer agent voice (2026-08-25) - the line every AI agent speaks at the talk close-up.
# Same policy as MrsHall: AI-generated (ElevenLabs), local-only, back up manually,
# regenerable from docs/DANCER_VOICE.md. Reaches the pak via DirectoriesToAlwaysCook.
Content/Audio/Dancers/
# Cinematic voice lines (kaia_intro etc.) - same AI-audio policy. Regenerable from
# Tools/Audio/*.mp3 via Tools/Scripts/import_cinematic_audio.py. See docs/CINEMATICS.md.
Content/Audio/Cinematics/
# AI Apparition clue voice (World 3) — AI-generated (ElevenLabs etc.); same policy as
# MrsHall: local-only + Drive backup, regenerable. Keep AI audio out of the public repo.
Content/AIApparition/S_ai_*

# --- Custom commissioned art (unless commissioned with full assignment) ---
Content/Commissioned/

# Keep folder structure visible to humans even when contents are ignored
!**/.gitkeep

# --- PCGExtendedToolkit (PCGEx) — bulky MIT third-party plugin source ---
#     Kept out of the repo for SIZE, not license (MIT permits redistribution).
#     Same re-clone-per-dev pattern as the Fab packs. To restore locally:
#       git clone --branch 5.7 https://github.com/PCGEx/PCGExtendedToolkit \
#         Plugins/PCGExtendedToolkit
#       git -C Plugins/PCGExtendedToolkit checkout 6912a2724
#     (UE 5.7 / EngineVersion 5.7.0; enabled via SibeliusGame.uproject.)
Plugins/PCGExtendedToolkit/

# UnrealClaude plugin build artifacts (CP2)
Plugins/UnrealClaude/Binaries/
Plugins/UnrealClaude/Intermediate/
Plugins/UnrealClaude/Resources/mcp-bridge/node_modules/

# Python bytecode cache (ue_bridge client runs under the engine's Python)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

