# Modular Library Tower (Stormcrow, Fab) — the Carousel of Fates room kit
Content/Library/

# BuildCookRun packaging logs (Tools/Scripts/package_v0*.ps1 output)
pkg-v*.log

# Exported devlog videos (belong in Videos/, not the repo)
/*.mp4

# Poly Supermarket 01 - the uFoods interior (docs/SPACEPORT_PLAN.md Phase E, the supply
# run). Bought from Fab, which buys USE and not REDISTRIBUTION, and this repo is public.
# Same rule as every other pack above: bytes stay local, re-install via Fab -> Add to
# Project on a fresh clone.
#
# It will reach the shipped pak through DirectoriesToAlwaysCook in DefaultGame.ini once
# L_uFoods actually uses it - Meshes and Materials, NOT Levels: the pack's L_Showcase and
# L_Overview are layout reference for building the interior, never something a player
# loads. That is exactly how the Rocket_Launch_Pad pack is handled.
Content/Poly_Supermarket_01/

# Build, package and commandlet logs written to the REPO ROOT by Tools/Scripts.
# Root-level only (/*.log), so nothing under Saved/ or Content/ is affected.
#
# 83 of these were already tracked when this rule was added (build-*.log, gate-*.log,
# pkg-v0*.log and friends) and they STAY tracked - a tracked file beats an ignore rule,
# and rewriting that much history to tidy up would cost more than the mess does. This
# only stops NEW ones being added.
#
# build-diag.log was untracked at the same time because it is the one that gets
# regenerated, so it showed as modified forever and hid real changes in git status.
/*.log

# ---- Elite Landscapes: Alien Part IV (Velarion, bought 2026-09-04) -----------
# Purchased vendor pack, 3.2 GB, and this repo is PUBLIC. It was NOT ignored on
# arrival - the same near-miss as Poly_Supermarket_01, which was one commit away
# from publishing a pack somebody paid for. Ignored before anything was staged.
#
# Six 8K landscape maps ship in it; docs/SEVENTH_POWER.md rev 3 wants exactly ONE
# for Grok. Only that map gets a +MapsToCook line, so the cooker follows only its
# references and the other five landscapes never reach the pak. A level hard-
# references what it places, so this needs no DirectoriesToAlwaysCook rule - the
# L_uFoods arrangement, not the Rocket_Launch_Pad one.
Content/Elite_AlienPack_04/
